(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-tanning-decision :finalize-tanning-operation :authorize-tanning-run :proceed-with-tanning-run :finalize-chemical-safety-clearance :declare-batch-safe-for-handling :declare-tanned-batch-safe-for-handling :declare-batch-safe-for-shipment :clear-batch-for-shipment :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "2799007521-cloud-itonami-isco-7521-wood-treaters-coverage" "2799007514-cloud-itonami-isco-7514-fruit-vegetable-preservers-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the tanning run" "proceed with the pelt tanning run" "authorize the tanning run" "authorize the pelt tanning run" "finalize the tanning decision" "finalize the tanning operation" "declare the batch safe for handling" "declare the tanned batch safe for handling" "declare the batch safe for shipment" "declare the tanned batch safe for shipment" "clear the batch for shipment" "clear the tanned batch for handling" "finalize the chemical safety clearance" "finalize the chemical-safety clearance" "declare the tannery chemical-safety cleared" "declare the tannery chemical safety cleared" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799007535), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}"), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/tannery-scheduling-logistics-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :tanner-verified :facility-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "7535"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007535: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7535 Pelt Dressers, Tanners and Fellmongers tannery scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7535\n-- Pelt Dressers, Tanners and Fellmongers** only, Wave3 (production/\ntrades) of the rollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3 batches 1-9\nalready landed: 54 occupations so far).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7535\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-occupation\n\\\"7535\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/technology`\nsibling present at the correct `../technology` relative path), and its\n`:name` read exactly \"Pelt Dressers, Tanners and Fellmongers\" --\nconfirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository\nexisted at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7535` (`gh api` 404\nconfirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `7535` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nPelt dressers, tanners and fellmongers process raw hides and pelts\nusing tanning chemicals (historically including chromium compounds and\nother hazardous agents) -- real chemical-exposure hazard, alongside\nbiological-material handling considerations. The controlling\nconstraint for this vertical is that the closed op allowlist must\nNEVER include any op that directly finalizes a tanning-execution\ndecision or a chemical-safety-clearance decision, nor override a shop\nsafety officer's judgment -- those decisions must always be a hard\npermanent block, never auto-commit-eligible. This actor is\ndeliberately scoped to TANNERY SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY\n-- it never performs tanning work or makes chemical-safety-clearance\ndecisions itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7521`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7521)\n(Wood Treaters: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split,\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same wave, a\nclosely-related chemical-processing-facility safety pattern --\ntreatment-execution finalization and chemical-safety-clearance\nexclusion, the same structural shape this vertical needs for\ntanning-execution and chemical-safety-clearance exclusion) -- cloned\nand read in full in this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7535` as an OSS tannery\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for pelt dressers, tanners and\nfellmongers, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as every\nprior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Tannery Scheduling\nCoordination Advisor ⊣ TanneryCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned\nidentically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different library\ncoordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated\n`20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **tannery scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct tanning-execution or chemical-safety-clearance\nauthority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate\nexercising, or propose exercising a tanning-execution decision, a\nchemical-safety-clearance decision, or any override of a shop safety\nofficer's judgment. These are not merely gated behind escalation --\nthey are structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- batch/inventory/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a chemical-exposure/ventilation/\n  equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit\n  eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- tanning-chemicals/raw-hide procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\ntanning-execution decision, a chemical-safety-clearance decision, or a\nshop-safety-officer-judgment override. These are **structurally absent\nfrom the op-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind escalation --\nan op such as `:finalize-tanning-decision` or\n`:declare-batch-safe-for-handling` cannot even be proposed by the\nreference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names eleven\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`tannerycoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-tanning-decision`, `:finalize-tanning-operation`,\n`:authorize-tanning-run`, `:proceed-with-tanning-run`,\n`:finalize-chemical-safety-clearance`,\n`:declare-batch-safe-for-handling`,\n`:declare-tanned-batch-safe-for-handling`,\n`:declare-batch-safe-for-shipment`, `:clear-batch-for-shipment`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`tannerycoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-tanning-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-tanning-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-tanning-run`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-tanning-run`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-chemical-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-batch-safe-for-handling`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-tanned-batch-safe-for-handling`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-batch-safe-for-shipment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-clear-batch-for-shipment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nplus actor-level integration coverage\n(`tannerycoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`,\n`.../holds-a-chemical-safety-clearance-op-even-at-high-confidence`,\n`.../holds-an-override-shop-safety-officer-op-even-at-high-confidence`).\n\n### Three HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable, plus the closed-allowlist check)\n\n1. **Tanner unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered tanner record (`:no-tanner`). Never trusts\n   the proposal's own claim of who the tanner is.\n2. **Facility unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered tannery site (`:no-facility`). Together\n   with check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that\n   a worker/facility record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the eleven\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with a\n   tanning run, declaring a batch safe for handling or shipment, or\n   overriding a shop safety officer's judgment, is a second HARD,\n   PERMANENT block (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated\n   unconditionally on content -- defense-in-depth on top of the\n   allowlist check: even if a future change somehow widened the\n   allowlist, content-based rejection still independently blocks\n   tanning-execution/chemical-safety-clearance/safety-override\n   language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a chemical-exposure/\n  ventilation/equipment-condition observation -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard\n  data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about shop safety or\n  batch clearance.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an\n  over-threshold tanning-chemicals/raw-hide order is not itself\n  unsafe, unlike a tanning-execution or chemical-safety-clearance\n  attempt, which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft\n  escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"pelt\", \"hide\", \"tanning\", \"chromium\") can accidentally match\ninside the mock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate\nproposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly\nthe risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a tannery coordination actor\nworking adjacent to chemical tanning work necessarily discusses those\nconcepts to do its scheduling/logging job) could trigger if phrased\ncarelessly. `tannerycoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased\nexclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the\ntanning run\", \"finalize the tanning operation\", \"declare the\ntanned batch safe for handling\", \"override the shop safety officer's\njudgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example phrasing), never\nbare nouns, and\n`tannerycoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for tanner ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for tannery\ntask ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer review\") WITHOUT\ncontaining any of the full finalization-action phrases, so the\nregression test is a genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-\nphrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on first run in this\nsession -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never\ntripped during development.\n`tannerycoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nand its chemical-safety-clearance/safety-officer-override siblings\nadditionally exercise the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7535\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7535` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7535`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 32 tests, 69 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-batch-clearance` that is\n  merely gated behind an always-escalate list: rejected outright per\n  the task's explicit domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op\n  still means the *capability* to finalize a chemical-safety-clearance\n  decision exists in the code path and is merely deferred to a human\n  gate. For a decision this severe (chemical-exposure and\n  biological-material-handling risk from tanning chemicals, including\n  historically toxic compounds such as chromium), the capability\n  itself must not exist. The only op related to shop-safety escalation\n  is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for human/shop-\n  safety-officer attention and never itself decides, authorizes, or\n  defers a tanning-execution or chemical-safety-clearance decision for\n  later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the\n  transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check used by some sibling actors):\n  rejected per the task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold\n  tanning-chemicals/raw-hide order is not itself unsafe, so it is\n  handled as a soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the\n  tanning-execution/chemical-safety-clearance/safety-officer-override\n  class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"pelt\" \"hide\"\n  \"tanning\" \"chromium\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known\n  self-trip bug class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked\n  example for this exact task), and per the explicit instruction to\n  phrase scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS,\n  never bare nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses\n  pelt/hide/tanning/chromium/safety-officer concepts to do its\n  scheduling/logging job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking\n  the actor's own legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly\n  against rationale text that deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Naming only a single tanning-execution-finalization op family\n  (mirroring a narrower single-category exclusion shape used by some\n  sibling actors): rejected -- the task's domain design names two\n  distinct excluded decision categories (tanning-execution,\n  chemical-safety-clearance) plus a shop-safety-officer-judgment\n  override, so this ADR and the governor's\n  `scope-excluded-ops`/`scope-excluded-phrases` name both explicitly\n  (with handling AND shipment clearance variants for the\n  chemical-safety-clearance category, since a tanned batch can be\n  declared safe for either purpose) rather than conflating them,\n  giving each its own dedicated unit test.\n- Merging `tanner` and `facility` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered tanner AND independently-registered\n  facility) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/facility\n  record must be independently verified/registered before any action\"\n  and the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- batch/inventory/progress data logging\n   only. Requires an independently registered tanner AND facility\n   (`:no-tanner`/`:no-facility`). Not a tanning-execution or\n   chemical-safety-clearance decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry a tanning-execution or chemical-safety-clearance\n   decision (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such\n   attempt via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action`\n   content check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any\n   conclusion about a specific tanning run or batch clearance -- it is\n   a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a chemical-exposure/\n   ventilation/equipment-condition concern to a human/shop safety\n   officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence\n   level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through\n   which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the shop safety\n   officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority, including\n   any chemical-safety-clearance decision.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- tanning-chemicals/raw-hide\n   procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not a tanning-execution,\n   chemical-safety-clearance or authorization decision of any kind --\n   it is a purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na tanning-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a specific\npelt-tanning run), a chemical-safety-clearance decision (e.g.\ndeclaring a tanned batch safe for handling or shipment), or a\nshop-safety-officer-judgment override -- these categories are\nstructurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op\nallowlist itself (`tannerycoord.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) eleven\nconcretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit\nlevel (`tannerycoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`tannerycoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-tanning-decision`\nand nine sibling tests), and (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check\nindependent of the `:op` field\n(`tannerycoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with a tanning run, finalize the tanning\noperation, declare a batch safe for handling or shipment, declare the\ntannery chemical-safety cleared, or override a shop safety officer's\njudgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`tannerycoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-tanning-run`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-chemical-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-finalize-tanning-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-declare-tannery-chemical-safety-cleared`).\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 32, :assertions 69, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Tannery Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :tanner-verification :facility-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7535"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7535"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7535)), (:test/simulator :tannerycoord.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7535 — Pelt Dressers, Tanners and Fellmongers Tannery Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7535)))
